{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what","id":824018,"title":"Oath of the Moon & Ghost Wolves and what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-04T22:27:07-08:00","id":824018,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Oath of the Moon & Ghost Wolves and what?","content":"So Oath of the Moon must be sworn after your first change. So ideally older werewolves come along and convince you to swear the oath.. How do they do it? Why would you swear an Oath to a strange magical being? I get it if you're found by a Tribe and they convince you to join their club, sure, as part of the joining you take up the Oath of the Moon... but what about Ghost Wolves? <br /> <br /> Why would they swear the Oath?They seem pretty reluctant to swear an Oath and bind themselves to a Tribe, why would they swear to the Moon?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:45:01-08:00","id":824032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what#post824018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would they swear the Oath?They seem pretty reluctant to swear an Oath and bind themselves to a Tribe, why would they swear to the Moon?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because the base contents of the Oath are literally just &quot;Do what you're metaphysically built to do, understand the role you play in that process, act appropriately for your relative standing with other werewolves, don't kill other werewolves, don't let humans find out you're a werewolf, and don't eat people.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T22:48:11-08:00","id":824033,"title":"","content":"It also reassures the locals that you aren't going to do those things, which relaxes some potential tensions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:11:36-08:00","id":824040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824032#post824032\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the base contents of the Oath are literally just &quot;Do what you're metaphysically built to do, understand the role you play in that process, act appropriately for your relative standing with other werewolves, don't kill other werewolves, don't let humans find out you're a werewolf, and don't eat people.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Why would you swear it? You're just fine _not_ doing it and be done with it? We're talking about those individuals who value their freedom and don't want to just swear loyalties. <br /> <br /> Will the Forsaken use force to get him to swear? <br /> <br /> The scenario which is coming up, is basically my players getting the First Change in play. And once Blood Talons or Storm Lords show up to tell them of their place in the world and get them to join the Forsaken, how would they convince them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:22:17-08:00","id":824043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824040#post824040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you swear it? You're just fine _not_ doing it and be done with it? We're talking about those individuals who value their freedom and don't want to just swear loyalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got a fucking moonsign stamped into your Essence. Loyalty has nothing to do with agreeing to abide by a relatively laissez-faire set of societal expectations in immediate proximity to a culture of supernatural busybodies who likely have a better handle on this whole &quot;being a goddamn werewolf&quot; business by virtue of simple trial-and-error and inertia.<br /> <br /> The way you've now framed this question is to ask why the Uratha equivalent of Mage's &quot;any rules at all are too stifling to countenance&quot; Scelesti would swear to do what their newfound magical nature drives them to do in a responsible manner.<br /> <br /> The Oath of the Moon is not a frontloaded aspect of werewolf cultural initiation and in all probability any pack that wants the new guy standing inside pissing out is going to bring it up after they've mentioned the whole &quot;if you don't balance your natures you're going to go on a killing spree and/or turn your neighborhood to shit&quot; part of the life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:41:42-08:00","id":824052,"title":"","content":"I think somewhere deep in the simple question thread this very idea is discussed. Ghost Wolves don't necessarily take the Oath of the Moon, or at least that's how I interpret it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11106-captain-shoe","name":"Captain Shoe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:43:48-08:00","id":824055,"title":"","content":"And consequently life can really suck for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:48:30-08:00","id":824056,"title":"","content":"Well, the book doesn't really present that as an option. Ghost Wolves are Forsaken, and that means they took the Oath. We know what happens if you don't - Silver deals more damage and you don't get your Auspice/Moon Gifts. <br /> <br /> And of course, for some it will be enough of a bribe - Swear this Oath which makes sense, to lessen some of your curses.<br /> But the book and setting leaves no room for those who refuse. We basically have two options before us.. Swear the Oath of the Moon and be Forsaken OR swear a different type of oath and be Pure. <br /> <br /> And this is throughout the world, some mystical force makes all the werewolves swear to somebody, something. I'm looking for a reason why, and why a stubborn werewolf (or a simple &quot;I don't wanna know any of your bullshit&quot;) would get in on the wagon. Especially if they have a pack of like-minded individuals to back them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T23:51:17-08:00","id":824058,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824056#post824056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the book doesn't really present that as an option. Ghost Wolves are Forsaken, and that means they took the Oath.</div> </div> </div> </div>It means they're not Pure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We know what happens if you don't - Silver deals more damage and you don't get your Auspice/Moon Gifts. </div> </div> </div>That's the consequences of being one of the Pure, which does not happen just because you don't swear the Oath, particularly given that the Pure swear a variant of the Oath anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T00:44:55-08:00","id":824088,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolves <i>character</i> <b>does not</b> swear Oaths of Moon and adhere to it's precepts - but it's still under Harmony-as-Trait mechanics rules.<br /> <br /> It's just like Scelasti in <b>Mage</b> - they can do not agree with any precepts of Wisdom Orders belive in - but still the are working under Wisdoms-as-Trait mechanics, in game, as rules. That mean that Scelast are very low-Wisdom mages - even if they do not belive in existance of Wisdom-as-Setting concept.<br /> <br /> Same is Ghosts Wolves - even if they do not &quot;belive&quot; in Oaths, breaking them lead them Harmony astray ( to side of Harmon 10 or Harmony 0 ).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T03:00:58-08:00","id":824139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824088#post824088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves <i>character</i> <b>does not</b> swear Oaths of Moon and adhere to it's precepts - but it's still under Harmony-as-Trait mechanics rules.<br /> <br /> It's just like Scelasti in <b>Mage</b> - they can do not agree with any precepts of Wisdom Orders belive in - but still the are working under Wisdoms-as-Trait mechanics, in game, as rules. That mean that Scelast are very low-Wisdom mages - even if they do not belive in existance of Wisdom-as-Setting concept.<br /> <br /> Same is Ghosts Wolves - even if they do not &quot;belive&quot; in Oaths, breaking them lead them Harmony astray ( to side of Harmon 10 or Harmony 0 ).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sadly, the Harmony specifically says, that breaking Oath of the Moon only applies to Forsaken. So no, you are not subject to Harmony breaking points from breaking the Oath before you actually take the Oath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:05:35-08:00","id":824158,"title":"","content":"Not taking the Oath of the Moon does not have any effect on silver damage or access to the Auspice. The Pure use an entirely different method of removing the Auspice from victims.<br /> <br /> Ghost Wolf groups with different beliefs and cults, like the Lodge of the Field, do not swear the Oath of the Moon. Ghost Wolves who never come into contact with wider Uratha society do not swear it. Numerous Ghost Wolves who are fully aware of Pure and Forsaken and who avoid or choose not to join the Forsaken also do not swear it. Ghost Wolves who accept the Urdaga orthodoxy but who fail to enter a Tribe or choose not to may well swear the Oath.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T04:42:36-08:00","id":824175,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">That directly contradicts what's written about the Pure. For example, let's take this from the recent blog about Pure: &quot;<span style=\"color:#555555\">The luckiest </span><i>Anshega</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#555555\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"> are discovered just prior to their first change, or immediately after before Luna can lay her claim. These Pure need never feel the shame of the moon\u2019s touch. Others aren\u2019t quite as fortunate. While they have broken Luna\u2019s chains, it was not before she could brand them with Auspice, which must be carefully, ritualistically \u2014 and excruciatingly \u2014 carved from the flesh and souls of these Uratha.&quot; <br /> <br /> That means that you don't have an Auspice upon First Change. You gain it afterwards, most likely with taking up the Oath. Of course, if after getting it you choose to go Pure - excruciating removal awaits, but if you never joined the Forsaken - there's nothing to remove. </span></span></span></span></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:22:37-08:00","id":824195,"title":"","content":"Or it means they just keep them inside. Or have a rite to forestall auspice brands, it does say 'immediately' after their first change, after all. Auspice branding might take two minutes. The idea that you don't get an auspice until you take the Oath is a rather large leap.<br /> <br /> Regarding the Ghost Wolves, it says, 'They\u2019re the werewolves who have rejected the Firstborn and turned their backs on Luna and the spirit courts alike.' Backing up the idea that they don't take the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Either way, it really doesn't sound like the Forsaken would use force to make someone swear the Oath. As Satchel has pointed out, they are fairly easy to abide by rules, and the idea that you're not going to swear an oath to not eat and murder people is probably enough to keep the Forsaken from wanting you with them. Though they might linger around if it looks like you plan on telling the world werewolves exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-05-2016, 08:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:29:24-08:00","id":824202,"title":"","content":"The lunar phase under which a werewolf has their First Change is explicitely tied to Auspice, and no such reference exists in second edition material in regards to the Oath of the Moon. The implication is that a werewolf's auspice proper is granted shortly after the First Change, so Pure who become aware of them prior have a certain facility in reaching the new uratha just before Luna can place her brand and consequently ensure she doesn't at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 02-05-2016, 08:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T05:56:15-08:00","id":824220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824202#post824202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lunar phase under which a werewolf has their First Change is explicitely tied to Auspice, and no such reference exists in second edition material in regards to the Oath of the Moon. The implication is that a werewolf's auspice proper is granted shortly after the First Change, so Pure who become aware of them prior have a certain facility in reaching the new uratha just before Luna can place her brand and consequently ensure she doesn't at all.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright. That makes sense. How does Luna placing her brand look like? Do Lunes come in and brand those werewolves shortly after the First Change? Within the same night perhaps? Does she do *magic BAM* you now have an Auspice? <br /> <br /> Rechecked the Oath, while most of them are common sense, and someone might swear that just because &quot;w/e, it's not like I'd like to do that anyways&quot; some of them don't seem to jive perfectly well with everyone. Like &quot;The Low Honor The High;The High Respect The Low&quot;, &quot;The Wolf Must Hunt&quot; and &quot;Respect Your Prey&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:13:05-08:00","id":824238,"title":"","content":"Magic Bam.<br /> <br /> There will probably be a period of time between the first change and the first dot of renown being granted. Perhaps removing an auspice before that occurs is far easier and less painful than stripping off brands. The alternative - that luna waits until <i>after</i> the change to grant auspice, and does not effectively do so the month before - is not something that has ever been suggested by the books. It certainly has nothing to do with the Oath though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:24:16-08:00","id":824246,"title":"","content":"The Wolf Must Hunt is a fact of life, like eating and drinking. If you don't do the Sacred Hunt, you begin losing an Essence per day and taking Breaking Points towards the Flesh, meaning you'll be unable to heal using Essence and be affected by your passive death rage trigger. Plus shapeshifting becomes much more difficult.<br /> <br /> But there's an entire group of werewolves, the Ghost Wolves, who refuse to follow the Oath. Some people clearly have issues with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T06:47:17-08:00","id":824258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824175#post824175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That means that you don't have an Auspice upon First Change. You gain it afterwards, most likely with taking up the Oath.</div> </div> </div> </div> Swearing the Oath has nothing to do with whether or not you acquire an Auspice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T07:52:07-08:00","id":824300,"title":"","content":"Alright. So how does gaining an Auspice work? Does it always, happen unless someone comes along who knows how to prevent it (Pure, most likely)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:10:34-08:00","id":824316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824300#post824300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. So how does gaining an Auspice work? Does it always, happen unless someone comes along who knows how to prevent it (Pure, most likely)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T08:23:09-08:00","id":824332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824300#post824300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright. So how does gaining an Auspice work? Does it always, happen unless someone comes along who knows how to prevent it (Pure, most likely)?</div> </div> </div> </div> Yup. Either someone who knows how to prevent it has to do so, or rare other circumstances might occur that cause the Auspice not to take or prevent it from taking. Such circumstances would probably be unique events that should be tailored by STs for their games and for specific plot reasons <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T09:57:45-08:00","id":824393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=824040#post824040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you swear it? You're just fine _not_ doing it and be done with it? We're talking about those individuals who value their freedom and don't want to just swear loyalties.<br /> <br /> Will the Forsaken use force to get him to swear?<br /> <br /> The scenario which is coming up, is basically my players getting the First Change in play. And once Blood Talons or Storm Lords show up to tell them of their place in the world and get them to join the Forsaken, how would they convince them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because werewolves are and deal with spiritual beings, things that follow a determinate set of rules and contracts, and it pays to display respect over taboos by acknowledging them formally.<br /> <br /> The use of force depends specifically on the NPCs.<br /> <br /> The way most Tribes get recruits is by leading by example, displaying their proficiency and having the cubs aspire to be as good as their potential mentors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T15:00:09-08:00","id":824611,"title":"","content":"What Ephsy said, adding that it's not a one-way street. Tribes want recruits, but new werewolves have a massive surge of instincts that make them want to form packs and hunt. The tribes offer ways of enabling both those things. Most werewolves are happy to join tribes, it feels right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:07:59-08:00","id":825480,"title":"","content":"I have a cosmetic question, what color does renown look on a Ghost Wolf? Blue/White for the Forsaken, Red for the Pure, but what for the Ghost? I am thinking dull Gray maybe? How else could a Pure and Spirit tell a Forsaken and Ghost apart......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3412-doctor-crimson","name":"Doctor Crimson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T11:33:55-08:00","id":825491,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure it's silver if you've got an auspice, red if you don't. There's no other distinction. <br /> <br /> In other words, you <i>can't </i>tell them apart, and that's why they often get lumped together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T13:18:34-08:00","id":825554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825491#post825491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure it's silver if you've got an auspice, red if you don't. There's no other distinction.<br /> <br /> In other words, you <i>can't </i>tell them apart, and that's why they often get lumped together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is accurate. The only observable distinction at that level between the Pure and every other werewolf is 'do you have an Auspice?'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T14:57:29-08:00","id":825613,"title":"","content":"Would I be correct in remembering hearing that the Pure outnumber the Forsaken?<br /> <br /> I suppose that's a different circumstance than Ghost Wolves but still implies some conclusions about the popularity of the Oaths, despite being so &quot;easy/convenient to follow&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T15:09:46-08:00","id":825618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825613#post825613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would I be correct in remembering hearing that the Pure outnumber the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>Varies by time and place, but the Brethren War definitely skewed the numbers that way in North American in the back half of the twentieth century.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I suppose that's a different circumstance than Ghost Wolves but still implies some conclusions about the popularity of the Oaths, despite being so &quot;easy/convenient to follow&quot; </div> </div> </div>It\u2026 actually has literally nothing to do with Ghost Wolves at that point, because the Pure's Oath only differs from the Forsaken's in who they're not allowed to kill and who they have to respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T15:10:02-08:00","id":825619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825613#post825613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would I be correct in remembering hearing that the Pure outnumber the Forsaken?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a first edition thing but not a given in second.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T15:49:45-08:00","id":825628,"title":"","content":"It's not like werewolves take censuses or anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T16:34:02-08:00","id":825652,"title":"","content":"Yes, though I wouldn't be surprised if the Ivory Claws kept as many records as possible, like the Mormon Geneaology Archives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T17:19:20-08:00","id":825668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825618#post825618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2026 actually has literally nothing to do with Ghost Wolves at that point, because the Pure's Oath only differs from the Forsaken's in who they're not allowed to kill and who they have to respect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, but some of those differences are some pretty big turn-offs compared to what the Oaths of the Moon ask","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T18:05:36-08:00","id":825681,"title":"","content":"Ghost Wolves could just be usurped by another being, or not know any better. Everyone who changes doesn't get a Forsaken, Pure or Bale Hound to guide them on the right path, some run into Lycaon-Ur, or a spirit who dominates them into obedience, or an idigam who eats their mind and soul and spits it back out with modifications. Some just languish in misunderstanding and loneliness until they snap and kill everyone they love, or fall into the Hisil forever.<br /> <br /> The three big Ghost Wolf groups we have are the Eaters of the Dead, the Lodge of the Field, and the poor bastards in Basra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 02-07-2016, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-07T23:16:11-08:00","id":825797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825681#post825681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves could just be usurped by another being, or not know any better. Everyone who changes doesn't get a Forsaken, Pure or Bale Hound to guide them on the right path, some run into Lycaon-Ur, or a spirit who dominates them into obedience, or an idigam who eats their mind and soul and spits it back out with modifications. Some just languish in misunderstanding and loneliness until they snap and kill everyone they love, or fall into the Hisil forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then there are the Australian ghost wolves who simply don't know about Firstborn or don't care about the beliefs of the non-native werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:30:31-08:00","id":825816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825681#post825681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghost Wolves could just be usurped by another being, or not know any better.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's exactly what happened with that one psychiatrist character in Hunting Grounds: the Rockies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T00:58:49-08:00","id":825829,"title":"","content":"So... again, since while a lot has been cleared up about the Pure and the Forsaken, I still don't see how The Ghost Wolves fit in. Obviously, they're lumped with the Forsaken due to Auspices. But how does that relate to the Oath of the Moon? And how do the Forsaken tell apart those who've taken the Oath and those who have not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:07:54-08:00","id":825835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825829#post825829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... again, since while a lot has been cleared up about the Pure and the Forsaken, I still don't see how The Ghost Wolves fit in. Obviously, they're lumped with the Forsaken due to Auspices. But how does that relate to the Oath of the Moon? And how do the Forsaken tell apart those who've taken the Oath and those who have not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The First Change is an event.<br /> <br /> It is not a subtle one.<br /> <br /> People notice, especially the invisible variety with a pseudosocietal preoccupation with oaths. Spirits talk to each other, and the broods of tribal totems are no exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:22:53-08:00","id":825839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825829#post825829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, they're lumped with the Forsaken due to Auspices. But how does that relate to the Oath of the Moon? And how do the Forsaken tell apart those who've taken the Oath and those who have not?</div> </div> </div> </div>As Oaths of Moons &quot;sins&quot; are <i>automatic</i> Breaking Points for the werewolf template - they <b><i>do not</i> need</b> to sweare Oaths of Moon to be under them. Forsaken and Pure only get Tribal Ban extra to all werewolves mechanics on Harmony.<br /> <br /> <b>All werewolves</b> go in to Spirit side when they eat wolves or human flesh. <br /> <br /> Harmony is template mechanics, not really relative in-game concept/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:22:22-08:00","id":825859,"title":"","content":"Well, that really depends on precisely what &quot;forsaken only&quot; means there. <br /> <br /> That said, the Oath is supposed to help with maintaining harmony, and if all it does is provide a new set of breaking points then it is objectively <i>not </i>doing that. You'd be better off never swearing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:41:54-08:00","id":825866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825839#post825839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Oaths of Moons &quot;sins&quot; are <i>automatic</i> Breaking Points for the werewolf template - they <b><i>do not</i> need</b> to sweare Oaths of Moon to be under them. Forsaken and Pure only get Tribal Ban extra to all werewolves mechanics on Harmony.<br /> <br /> <b>All werewolves</b> go in to Spirit side when they eat wolves or human flesh.<br /> <br /> Harmony is template mechanics, not really relative in-game concept/</div> </div> </div> </div>Breaking the Oath of The Moon breaking points, is specifically written as Forsaken only. So that means that only those who've swore it are Forsaken.<br /> <br /> And that's exactly the problem I'm having at the moment. Where do Ghost Wolves who never swear an oath fit into this?<br /> <br /> And sure enough, eating humans could be a generic breaking point, for all werewolves.. but some other tenants of the Oath have no reason to do so. Since not all the points of the Oath are generic &quot;this totally makes sense&quot; things. Some of them are not. And of course, if all those tenants where equal to all werewolves and breaking points to all, thus making the oath just naming of them out loud.. why don't the Pure suffer from them?<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, the Pure take up their own version of the Oath, so they do probably get some of those applied on them too. But is it identical? just sworn to a different entity? If so, then it could make sense, that those are generic breaking points for everybody.. different factions just frame them differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T02:46:45-08:00","id":825870,"title":"","content":"If you could compile list of list of Harmony Breakig Points that are based on the Oaths I would point you which are for all Uratha, and what are only for Tribes. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:01:45-08:00","id":825876,"title":"","content":"Sure. So, the breaking point in question is listed in the book as:<br /> \u2022 Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132) <br /> <br /> Now let's list what's Oath of the Moon from the book:<br /> The people do not murder the people;<br /> The Wolf Must Hunt<br /> The low honor the high, the high respect the low;<br /> Respect your Prey;<br /> Do not eat the flesh of man or wolf;<br /> The herd must not know<br /> The Uratha shall cleave to the human;<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:11:32-08:00","id":825883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2022 Violating the Oath of the Moon. (Forsaken only, \u20132)</div> </div> </div> </div>I will mark &quot;<b>instinctive</b>&quot; as those that are unversal for all Uratha, Ghost Wolves also. They are base of werewolf template, really, not only tradition of the Tribes. Those marked as <b>tribal </b>are only from culture of Tribes - and so Forsaken and Pure specific.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The people do not murder the people;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would bet it's <b>instinctive</b> one - but Pure have different freasing of it. Well, maybe their Oaths of Wolf change a bit spectrum of this particular Breaking Point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wolf Must Hunt</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly <b>instinctive</b> one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The low honor the high, the high respect the low;</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Tribal</b> Breaking Point - Ghost Wolves would be free from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Respect your Prey;</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Tribal </b>Breaking Point - Ghost Wolves would be free from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not eat the flesh of man or wolf;</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly <b>instinctive</b> one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The herd must not know</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Tribal</b> Breaking Point - Ghost Wolves would be free from them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825876#post825876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Uratha shall cleave to the human;</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly <b>instinctive</b> one.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T03:32:14-08:00","id":825892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825883#post825883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt; The Uratha shall cleave to the human<br /> <br /> Clearly <b>instinctive</b> one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree with this one... because why would forsaking humanity and going all out spirit, would cause you to break towards *flesh* as it does now?<br /> <br /> But sure, houseruling this, and separating the Oath Breaking points into instinctive and actually Oath bound makes sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T04:34:08-08:00","id":825916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825829#post825829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... again, since while a lot has been cleared up about the Pure and the Forsaken, I still don't see how The Ghost Wolves fit in. Obviously, they're lumped with the Forsaken due to Auspices. But how does that relate to the Oath of the Moon? And how do the Forsaken tell apart those who've taken the Oath and those who have not?</div> </div> </div> </div>They can't tell.<br /> <br /> I think the comment about Forsaken Only on the Oath of the Moon Breaking Point was in order to leave it open for future different elements for other factions, like the Pure's own Oath, not to indicate that Ghost Wolf characters are unaffected.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:16:25-08:00","id":825928,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Ghost Wolves are there as a wildcard for Forsaken players, capable of being enemies or allies or simply obstacles, but also allow you to play 'tribeless' games if you want to play one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T05:35:51-08:00","id":825934,"title":"","content":"Alright, thanks for the answers. This did clear up quite a few things for me about Werewolf <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T06:28:26-08:00","id":825965,"title":"","content":"Violating Oath of the Moon is clearly Forsaken only because <i>that's what it says</i>. How is anything regarding that single breaking point debatable?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T07:46:39-08:00","id":825983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825652#post825652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, though I wouldn't be surprised if the Ivory Claws kept as many records as possible, like the Mormon Geneaology Archives.</div> </div> </div> </div>The central Ivory Claw genealogy archive would have to have security that would make the Mormon archive's <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_23490_6-super-secure-places-protecting-shockingly-stupid-things.html\" target=\"_blank\">over the top security</a> look like a suburban bank branch in a GTA game. Which means that it's a perfect target for a pack of PCs to heist their way into (perhaps to screw with the records of a ivory claw family that's been causing problems for them.).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T07:55:24-08:00","id":825989,"title":"","content":"Yeah. Still, I could see it being important to them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Forsaken could try and get information released willingly, jumping through hoops to find out their lineage. Wouldn't it be disrespecting someone else's heritage to not give them the chance to honor it? I also like the dichotomy. They honor Father Wolf, and so have records of as many werewolves as they can find, but in doing so they risk a massive breach of 'The Herd Must Not Know,' as well as potentially having something found that, if in the hands of the enemies of the Uratha, would give them a kill list.<br /> <br /> I keep imagining the Ivory Claws to be cutting edge, tech-wise. Presumably because they 'move among the wealthy and powerful.' I could see it as a point of contention with the Predator Kings, but I like the fact that Technology isn't one of their tribal gifts, so they aren't as naturally fluent at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T08:09:29-08:00","id":825995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825983#post825983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The central Ivory Claw genealogy archive would have to have security that would make the Mormon archive's <a href=\"http://www.cracked.com/article_23490_6-super-secure-places-protecting-shockingly-stupid-things.html\" target=\"_blank\">over the top security</a> look like a suburban bank branch in a GTA game. Which means that it's a perfect target for a pack of PCs to heist their way into (perhaps to screw with the records of a ivory claw family that's been causing problems for them.).</div> </div> </div> </div>I always imagined there were more than one 'central' archive. For example, in my own games there are actually three of them that all share identical information. The risk of the enemy getting their hands upon them is dangerous, certainly, but not as terrible as the risk of losing the information entirely. These records are cross referenced once a month with smaller archives to maintain accuracy, then cross referenced with the two central archives once a year (or when an audit is requested by an Ivory Claw elder). One of these is an archive of Teotihuacan codices, another is a cluster of servers running in a cold room, and the third is an ancient Akkadian spirit who memorizes everything through oral tradition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T08:48:38-08:00","id":826011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/824018-oath-of-the-moon-ghost-wolves-and-what?p=825989#post825989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. Still, I could see it being important to them.<br /> <br /> Alternatively Forsaken could try and get information released willingly, jumping through hoops to find out their lineage. Wouldn't it be disrespecting someone else's heritage to not give them the chance to honor it? I also like the dichotomy. They honor Father Wolf, and so have records of as many werewolves as they can find, but in doing so they risk a massive breach of 'The Herd Must Not Know,' as well as potentially having something found that, if in the hands of the enemies of the Uratha, would give them a kill list.<br /> <br /> I keep imagining the Ivory Claws to be cutting edge, tech-wise. Presumably because they 'move among the wealthy and powerful.' I could see it as a point of contention with the Predator Kings, but I like the fact that Technology isn't one of their tribal gifts, so they aren't as naturally fluent at it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I kinda like the idea of the Ivory Claws reluctantly letting forsaken look up their own lineage in their archives, to be honest. They probably wouldn't let them into one of the central archives, but would probably let them into the branch offices in exchange for said forsaken doing some slightly unplesent favors for the claws.<br /> <br /> And Incendax is right, they probably do have more than one central archive, along with hidden subsections in mundane genealogy archives such as the Mormon one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T09:00:09-08:00","id":826860,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of Ivory Claws as Mormon evangelists who knock on your door even better. I can see them waltzing into your pack's territory and going, &quot;Lo, and these are the works of your father before you, and his father before him, and if you don't honor these deeds, we're going to tear you a new one.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-15T17:30:04-08:00","id":830632,"title":"","content":"That's actually something that is addressed in the game that I am running now.<br /> <br /> I really like to add complexity to stuff to make it seem more realistic (in my opinion), so depending on your location the Oath of the Moon is interpreted differently. In Chicago and much of the Midwest, the Oath of the Moon has a sort of religious, doctrinal component to it - there are just certain things that you shouldn't ever do (in theory) like using silver, or eating the flesh of humans, or using rituals to bind spirits and create Ridden. That's some serious, hardcore <b>heresy</b>, but let's face it - sometimes things aren't always so cut and dry and easy as that.<br /> <br /> I find the Forsaken too often portrayed as the good guys and after a while that got boring for me. I think making the Oath of the Moon doctrinal, and having the consequences of violation be expulsion, or beating, or shunning, or marking, etc., makes it a little easier for me to believe that someone would swear the Oath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3028-viskarenvisla","name":"viskarenvisla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3028_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}